        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "49eae371-1fb9-5aae-9766-a3833cd7931e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Operations: Operation Phantom Linebacker\n- Military units: U.S. 3rd Brigade, 2nd Infantry Division\n- Organizations: Iraqi National Guard, Iraqi Border Police, Multinational Forces, United States Army, United States Forces Korea\n- Places: Iraq, Syria, South Korea\n\nFacts:\n- Operation Phantom Linebacker was a coalition military operation in Iraq designed to interdict anti-government fighters from entering Iraq from Syria.\n- The U.S. 3rd Brigade and the 2nd Infantry Division conducted Operation Phantom Linebacker with the Iraqi National Guard, Iraqi Border Police, and other Multinational Forces.\n- The 2nd Infantry Division, also called Indianhead, 2ID, 2nd ID, and Second D, is a formation of the United States Army.\n- The 2nd Infantry Division has approximately 17,000 soldiers, and about 10,000 of them are stationed in South Korea.\n- The soldiers stationed in South Korea account for about 35% of United States Forces Korea personnel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "71e6ddef-39a8-5f62-83e9-d52e73d0a9bb",
        "text": "Page: Operation Phantom Linebacker. Sentence: Operation Phantom Linebacker was a coalition military operation in Iraq designed to interdict anti-government fighters from entering Iraq from Syria.\nPage: Operation Phantom Linebacker. Sentence: The U.S. 3rd Brigade and the 2nd Infantry Division (United States) conducted the operation with the Iraqi National Guard, Iraqi Border Police, and other Multinational Forces.\nPage: 2nd Infantry Division (United States). Sentence: The 2nd Infantry Division (\"Indianhead\"; \"2ID,\" \"2nd ID\", or \"Second D\") is a formation of the United States Army.\nPage: 2nd Infantry Division (United States). Sentence: There are approximately 17,000 soldiers in the 2nd Infantry Division, with 10,000 of them stationed in South Korea, accounting for about 35% of the United States Forces Korea personnel.",
